<title>GERMANY: German Dec import prices +0.8 pct m/m, +2.0 y/y.</title>
<headline>German Dec import prices +0.8 pct m/m, +2.0 y/y.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN TRADE PRICES    Dec 96	Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p>IMPORT prices:</p>
<p>    Monthly figure	  +0.8	  +0.0	 +0.3</p>
<p>    Year-on-year	    +2.0	  +1.4	 -0.9</p>
<p>    Index(base 100 1991)  99.0	  98.2	 97.1</p>
<p>EXPORT prices:</p>
<p>    Monthly figure	  +0.1	  -0.1	 -0.1</p>
<p>    Year-on-year	    +0.3	  +0.1	 +0.7</p>
<p>    Index(base 100 1991) 103.5	 103.4	103.2</p>
<p>NOTE - The office said that for the full year 1996, import prices showed an average rise of 0.5 percent. Export prices showed an average rise of 0.2 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
